scaleplex: vf_inlineass CUDA branch — GPU-resident text/ASS sub-burn (#76)

Adds a CUDA hardware branch to vf_inlineass, mirroring the VAAPI branch.
libass renders the active cue at render_height into a straight-alpha RGBA
buffer; swscale upscales+converts it to a full-frame YUVA420P CUDA overlay
surface; a per-plane alpha-blend kernel (adapted verbatim from
vf_overlay_cuda.cu, LGPL-2.1) composites it onto the CUDA video frame in
place. Eliminates the per-frame full-frame hwdownload the interim NVIDIA
sub-burn path required (worker subBurnDownloadFilter -> "").

Text/ASS only; bitmap (PGS) on CUDA is out of scope for now. All new code +
the .ptx/load_helper objects are gated on CONFIG_OVERLAY_CUDA_FILTER.

Index: ffmpeg/libavfilter/Makefile
===================================================================
--- ffmpeg.orig/libavfilter/Makefile
+++ ffmpeg/libavfilter/Makefile
@@ -363,6 +363,14 @@ OBJS-$(CONFIG_IDENTITY_FILTER)
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_IDET_FILTER)                   += vf_idet.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_IL_FILTER)                     += vf_il.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_INLINEASS_FILTER)              += vf_inlineass.o vaapi_vpp.o
+# scaleplex (issue #76): inlineass CUDA branch. inlineass is always built, but
+# the .cu -> .ptx rule needs nvcc, so the ptx + load_helper objects are gated
+# on CONFIG_OVERLAY_CUDA_FILTER (== 1 only when nvcc is present and CUDA filters
+# build) — the SAME guard as the #if CONFIG_OVERLAY_CUDA_FILTER C code. A
+# CUDA-less build sees neither the objects nor the C branch. OBJS is sorted +
+# deduped in common.mak, so cuda/load_helper.o (also added by overlay_cuda)
+# collapses to a single entry.
+OBJS-$(CONFIG_OVERLAY_CUDA_FILTER)           += vf_inlineass_cuda.ptx.o cuda/load_helper.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_INFLATE_FILTER)                += vf_neighbor.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_INTERLACE_FILTER)              += vf_tinterlace.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_INTERLEAVE_FILTER)             += f_interleave.o
